-#
  Two mutually exclusive indicators, both pinned to the bottom left corner, so only one may render:
  a loud banner naming the running version on the staging server (see ApplicationHelper#staging?),
  and, everywhere else, a small build stamp for editors and admins that expands on click. The latter
  is a plain <details> element, so it needs no JavaScript.
- if staging?
  .staging-version-indicator= t(:staging_version, version: deployment_version)
- elsif show_deployment_version?
  %details.deployment-version-indicator{ dir: 'ltr' }
    %summary{ title: t(:deployment_version_title) }= deployment_sha.to_s[0, 8].presence || t(:version_unknown)
    %dl.deployment-version-details
      %dt= t(:deployment_commit)
      %dd
        - if deployment_commit_url.present?
          = link_to deployment_sha, deployment_commit_url, target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener'
        - else
          = t(:version_unknown)
      %dt= t(:deployment_committed_at)
      %dd
        - if deployment_time.present?
          %time{ datetime: deployment_time.iso8601 }= deployment_time.in_time_zone.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z')
        - else
          = t(:version_unknown)
